  "id": "diversion-program",
  "term": "diversion program",
  "definition": "A diversion program is a structured support service for individuals and families dealing with problems such as substance misuse, behavior difficulties, or legal troubles. It typically provides guidance, referrals, case management, advocacy, and short-term support to help people understand their problems, connect with suitable services, and work toward positive change while protecting public safety.",
